From 379dcf4a3193760d81a0fbc0dde32f272a9fb45c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ragavan <rramasamy@maxlinear.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:25:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] genEvt: set channel change reason to DFS for
 radar-triggered channel switches

When a channel change is triggered by radar detection (DFS), the
channel change event was incorrectly reported with reason "AUTO".

This happens because hostapd continues to report ACS as the configured
channel selection method even after a radar hit causes the AP to move
to a different channel. As a result, pWHM classifies the channel
change as AUTO instead of DFS.

Fix this by checking whether the current chanspec is affected by radar
at the time of the channel change. If radar is detected on the current
channel, update the channel change reason to DFS.

This ensures radar-triggered channel switches are reported with the
correct reason.

Closes: PPW-2490
Signed-off-by: Ragavan Ramasamy <rramasamy@maxlinear.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.com/prpl-foundation/prplmesh/pwhm/plugins/pwhm/-/commit/d98e8724c41ad2d7a19d437e70dce132201fc181]
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
index 33b22891f3f516dcb95cc174b195743d7d951e6b..28cd1f26348491c5a3f0d1582eca768a2e595a95 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c
@@ -135,6 +135,9 @@ static const char* s_fwdRadioStdWpaCtrlEventsList[] = {
 static wld_channelChangeReason_e s_getLastAppliedChanReason(T_Radio* pRad) {
     ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pRad, CHAN_REASON_UNKNOWN, ME, "Null rad");
     wld_channelChangeReason_e reason = pRad->targetChanspec.reason;
+    if(wld_channel_is_radar_detected(pRad->currentChanspec.chanspec)) {
+        return CHAN_REASON_DFS;
+    }
     if(pRad->autoChannelSupported && pRad->autoChannelEnable) {
         if(wld_rad_hostapd_hasCfgAcs(pRad)) {
             reason = CHAN_REASON_AUTO;
